Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Phase II Rung 2: eps!=0 ice-split hand-check (b) + clean
 Rung-1 fixture

Note 1 -- hand-check (b), the last unverified corner of the core physics. Ice
conservation and the rate gate are both eps=0 or eps-independent, so neither can
catch an ice split that uses the wrong redistribution weight. tests/coag_ice_check
verifies, on the 3-bin toy, a genuine eps=0.5 pair:
  (1,2): m+ = m1+m2 = 3 m1 in [m2=2m1, m3=4m1] => eps=(4-3)/(4-2)=0.5 into bins 2,3
and asserts the ice reaction J01CO+GRAIN02 -> 0.5 J02CO + 0.5 J03CO + GRAIN02 has
product weights IDENTICAL to the grain reaction GRAIN01+GRAIN02 -> 0.5 GRAIN02 +
0.5 GRAIN03 (ice-follows-particle, same eps), plus the catalyst GRAIN02 (weight 1)
and the eps=0 clean merge (1,1) depositing all to bin 2. PASS.

Note 2 -- tests/fixture_dust_coag now lists BASE grain species GRAIN0/GRAIN- and
lets read_species expand them per bin (as it always should have; the earlier
explicit per-bin listing produced duplicate + null species slots). Clean 36-species
list now. All Rung 1/1b gates unchanged: constant gate (b1) 9.8e-6, Brownian gate
early-slope 4.7e-5, kernel check 1e-11, coag-OFF byte-identical.
